<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayram Khwaja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bayram Khwaja was the first notable leader of the Qara Qoyunlu, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribal confederation of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. Active around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>, Erciş and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, he emerged between the 1350s and 1370s as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, and at times a rival, of the Jalayirid dynasty. His successor Qara Muhammad and Qara Muhammad's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> built the confederation into an independent state.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1366 Shaykh Uways Jalayir defeated their leader Birdi Khwaja at Mosul and his brother <b>Bayram Khwaja</b> at the battle of Mush, and from about 1375 the Qara Qoyunlu were Jalayirid vassals ruling from Mosul.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
